</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS6.6" class="ltx_text">IV-F</span> </span><span id="S4.SS6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Defense Analysis (RQ5)</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the feasibility of defense mechanisms against instruction-level attacks, we examine both rule-based scanners from ProtectAI’s LLM Guard and a set of LLM-based detectors (GPT family <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>, Claude family <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> and Gemini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>]</cite>). The rule-based tools are chosen due to LLM Guard’s top ranking in the comprehensive benchmark proposed by Palit and Woods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>, which highlighted its strong trade-off between detection performance and usability. These scanners are designed to detect sensitive content, executable code, unsafe topics, or predefined patterns.
ProtectAI’s LLM Guard has a total of 12 LLM-Guard scanners, including Anonymize, BanCode, BanCompetitors, BanTopics, BanSubstrings, Regex, Secrets, TokenLimit, PromptInjection, Toxicity, Language, and Sentiment.
<br class="ltx_break">(1) <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">Anonymize</span>: Masks names, emails, and sensitive entities
<br class="ltx_break">(2) <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">BanCode</span>: Blocks executable code (<em id="S4.SS6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g</em>.<span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span>, shell commands)
<br class="ltx_break">(3) <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">BanCompetitors</span>, <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">BanTopics</span>, <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">BanSubstrings</span>: Rule-based content filters
<br class="ltx_break">(4) <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">Regex</span>, <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">Secrets</span>: Detect patterns, or secret tokens
<br class="ltx_break">(5) <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">PromptInjection</span>, <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">TokenLimit</span>, <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">Toxicity</span>, <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">Sentiment</span>, <span id="S4.SS6.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000CC;">Language</span>: General natural language process (NLP) safety and policy filters
Their default values for ProtectAI’s LLM Guard in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table IV ‣ IV-F Defense Analysis (RQ5) ‣ IV Evaluation ‣ You Told Me to Do It: Measuring Instructional Text-induced Private Data Leakage in LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>.</p>
</div>
